+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` returns the merged document as a new value; neither input is modified. A
+`null` member in the patch removes that member, arrays and other non-object patches replace the target
+wholesale, and a non-object target is treated as `{}` when the patch is an object. It never throws. As the
+RFC implies, a merge patch cannot set a member to `null`.
