@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/patch.ts` and `src/pointer.ts` follow a pattern: one module per RFC, re-exported from `src/index.ts`, no dependencies, inputs never mutated. Inputs are plain parsed JSON values.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** a faithful RFC 7386 `MergePatch` algorithm; pure function; safe against `__proto__` keys.
+**Non-Goals:** generating merge patches from two documents; error class (the RFC defines no failure cases).
+
+## Decisions
+
+- New `src/merge-patch.ts` with a recursive function mirroring the RFC pseudocode. Non-object targets become `{}`; results are built into fresh objects, and values taken from the patch are deep-copied (with nulls stripped when merged into `{}`, per the RFC recursion), so nothing is shared.
+- Own members are copied with `Object.defineProperty`-style assignment so a `__proto__` key becomes an ordinary own property.
+- "Object" means non-null, non-array `typeof "object"`.
+- No validation or throwing: any JSON value is a legal patch.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- A `null` cannot be set as a member value through a merge patch; this is inherent to RFC 7386 and is documented in the README.
